# Reviewed comparisons with an encoded column (scripts/check-sql-boundary.py).
# One per line: <path relative to crates/kutup-server>|<the matched text>.
# Each needs a reason: the row is already found by a key, so no index is lost.
#
# account_devices.rs: the device row is found by (account_id, device_id); this
# only checks it against its manifest entry (a 32-byte key).
src/account_devices.rs|= kutup_b64(d.frame_key)
